Step 1: Write down the correct formula for the area of a circle.

$$
A  = \pi \times r^{2}
$$

Step 2: Substitute the correct values into the formula. Use 3.14 for $\pi$.

$$
\begin{align}
 A  &= \pi \times r^{2}\\
  & = 3.14 \times \text{7}^{2}
\end{align}
$$

Step 3: Do the calculation and remember to show the correct units in your answer.

$$
\begin{align}
 A & = \pi \times r^{2}\\
 &= 3.14 \times \text{7}^{2} \\
 &= 3.14 \times \text{49}\\
 &= \text{153.86} \text{ mm$^{2}$}
\end{align}
$$

